{
  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST find an ancestor containing both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`, require a nonempty relative mdBook source path without parent components and a `SUMMARY.md` at that path, and report an error when these prerequisites are absent or invalid.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The core implementation matches the requirement. Part of it is only cited rather than marked `{impl}`, and two parts of the requirement have no test marked for it.\n\n**What is implemented correctly**\n- `find_project_root` (src/setup.rs:56) walks `cwd.ancestors()` for a directory holding both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`.\n- `project_root` (src/setup.rs:66) reports \"cannot find a project with Cargo.toml and book.toml\" when none is found.\n- `book_source` (src/setup.rs:35) defaults to `src` only when the `book` table or `book.src` is absent. It errors when `book` is not a table or `book.src` is not a string.\n- `run` (src/setup.rs:97-110) rejects an empty source. It also rejects any path component other than `Normal` or `CurDir`, which excludes absolute, parent and prefix components. It then requires `SUMMARY.md` in the source directory.\n- The extra behaviour in `run` (CSS, dev-dependency, test file) is covered by other requirements: `setup_css`, `setup_local_path` and `setup`.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. **Partial implementation with only `{cite}`.** `is_configured` (src/setup.rs:~177-205) re-implements the same checks: `book_source`, the empty-source test, the component whitelist and the `SUMMARY.md` check. It is marked only `{cite}` for `requirements.cli.setup_project`. Per the criteria, code that implements part of the requirement without `{impl}` is a gap.\n2. **Missing test for ancestor discovery and the missing-project error.** The only tests marked `{test}` for this requirement are in tests/setup.rs: `setup_uses_src_when_book_table_or_source_setting_is_absent` and `setup_rejects_invalid_book_configuration`. Neither runs `habeas setup` from a subdirectory. Neither runs it with `Cargo.toml` or `book.toml` missing from every ancestor to check the \"cannot find a project\" error. A test of that error exists at tests/commands.rs:~574, but it has no `{test}` link to `setup_project`. The session-start test at tests/setup.rs:~205 covers a nested directory, but it belongs to the hook requirement.\n3. **Untested invalid-path variants.** The test covers an empty source, `/outside` and `../outside`. The remaining accepted forms (`./x`, nested paths) and the case where only one of the two files exists are not covered.\n\nThese gaps are not acknowledged by any FIXME, so the determination is false.",
